.TH QUANUXCTL-SSH 8 "August 2026" "QuanuX System Manager" "QuanuX Deployment Documentation"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-ssh \- Execute a deployed payload via Conditioned SSH Execution.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquanuxctl -ssh\fR [\fIHOSTNAME\fR] [\fIPAYLOAD_NAME\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBquanuxctl -ssh\fR initiates a secure shell connection to a Tier 2-4 edge node to execute a staged payload.
The execution is strictly governed by the \fBTrue Sovereign Lifecycle\fR. The Native Envoy strictly gates
execution by verifying capabilities and dynamically generating a shell wrapper. 
.PP
If the prerequisite Handshake and Out-of-Band (OOB) deploy sequence were not completed, or if the \fIhabitat.json\fR 
violates the capability registry, the execution wrapper will not exist, resulting in a physical rejection.
.SH PHYSICS & MECHANISM
The C++ Native Envoy utilizes the \fBDumb Courier\fR pattern. The python execution CLI constructs the capability hooks 
(e.g., \fInumactl\fR, \fIonload\fR) and passes them to the Envoy during the payload transfer. The Envoy writes the 
hook into \fB/opt/quanux/payloads/.run_<payload>.sh\fR and authenticates it with POSIX chmod constraints.
.SH EXAMPLES
quanuxctl -ssh tier4-node01 striker_dma
.SH SEE ALSO
quanuxctl-telemetry(8), native-envoy(8)
